Nothing here is real, and nothing here leaves your phone.

s3mail reads mail that Amazon SES writes into an S3 bucket you own. No
server in between, no mailbox on somebody else's machine: the bucket is
yours, and this app talks to it directly.

To use it for real you need two things - an AWS account with a bucket set
up for SES, and the s3mail desktop program, which hands this phone a
pairing code. Everything else it works out on its own.

Have a look around. Swipe a message, open the newsletter, tap the star.
It all behaves exactly as it does with real mail, because it is the same
code underneath.
